[al:新概念英语第四册]
[ar: New Concept English]
[ti: Education]
[by: Generated by iChochy]
[00:00.94]Lesson 33 | 第33课
[00:03.04]Education | 教育
[00:10.92]Why is education democratic in bookless tribal societies? | 为什么在没有书籍的部落社会中，教育是民主的？
[00:18.65]Education is one of the key words of our time. | 教育是我们这个时代的一个关键词。
[00:23.29]A man without an education, many of us believe, | 我们许多人认为，一个没有受过教育的人
[00:27.40]is an unfortunate victim of adverse circumstances, deprived of one of the greatest twentieth-century opportunities. | 是不幸境遇的受害者，被剥夺了20世纪最宝贵的机会之一。
[00:37.15]Convinced of the importance of education, modern states 'invest' in institutions of learning to get back 'interest' | 现代国家深信教育的重要性，因此“投资”于教育机构，以期获得“回报”
[00:46.84]in the form of a large group of enlightened young men and women who are potential leaders. | 这种回报就是培养出一大批开明的青年男女，他们都是潜在的领导者。
[00:53.93]Education, with its cycles of instruction so carefully worked out, | 教育有着精心设计的教学周期，
[00:59.35]punctuated by textbooks—those purchasable wells of wisdom—what would civilization be like without its benefits? | 并以教科书——那些可以买到的智慧源泉——作为点缀。如果没有教育的这些益处，文明将会是什么样子？
[01:10.77]So much is certain: that we would have doctors and preachers, | 有一点是肯定的：我们仍然会有医生和传教士，
[01:16.51]lawyers and defendants, marriages and births—but our spiritual outlook would be different. | 律师和被告、婚姻和生育——但我们的精神观念将会有所不同。
[01:25.07]We would lay less stress on 'facts and figures' and more on a good memory, | 我们会较少强调“事实和数据”，而更多地重视良好的记忆力，
[01:31.53]on applied psychology, and on the capacity of a man to get along with his fellow-citizens. | 重视应用心理学，以及一个人与同胞和睦相处的能力。
[01:39.04]If our educational system were fashioned after its bookless past we would have the most democratic form of 'college' imaginable. | 如果我们的教育体系仿照过去没有书籍的社会来建立，我们就会拥有可以想象得到的最民主的“大学”形式。
[01:50.08]Among tribal people all knowledge inherited by tradition is shared by all; | 在部落民族中，所有通过传统继承的知识都由全体成员共享；
[01:56.92]it is taught to every member of the tribe so that in this respect everybody is equally equipped for life. | 这些知识传授给部落的每一个成员，因此在这方面，每个人都同样具备了应对生活的能力。
[02:06.45]It is the ideal condition of the 'equal start' which only our most progressive forms of modern education try to regain. | 这就是“平等起步”的理想状态，只有我们最先进的现代教育形式才试图重新实现这一点。
[02:17.00]In primitive cultures the obligation to seek and to receive the traditional instruction is binding to all. | 在原始文化中，寻求和接受传统教育是每个人都必须履行的义务。
[02:25.63]There are no 'illiterates'—if the term can be applied to peoples without a script—while our own compulsory school attendance became law in Germany in 1642, | 那里没有“文盲”——如果这个词可以用于没有文字的民族的话——而我们自己的义务入学制度于1642年在德国成为法律，
[02:39.77]in France in 1806, and in England in 1876 and is still nonexistent in a number of 'civilized' nations. | 1806年在法国成为法律，1876年在英国成为法律，而一些所谓的“文明”国家至今仍未实行这一制度。
[02:51.14]This shows how long it was before we deemed it necessary to make sure | 这表明，我们花了很长时间才认识到有必要确保
[02:56.66]that all our children could share in the knowledge accumulated by the 'happy few' during the past centuries. | 所有孩子都能分享过去几个世纪由“少数幸运儿”积累的知识。
[03:07.21]Education in the wilderness is not a matter of monetary means. | 荒野中的教育并不取决于金钱。
[03:12.73]All are entitled to an equal start. | 所有人都有权获得平等的起点。
[03:16.37]There is none of the hurry which, in our society, often hampers the full development of a growing personality. | 那里没有我们社会中常见的那种匆忙，而这种匆忙往往妨碍一个成长中的人格得到充分发展。
[03:26.13]There, a child grows up under the ever-present attention of his parents; | 在那里，孩子在父母始终如一的关怀下成长；
[03:32.11]therefore the jungles and the savannahs know of no 'juvenile delinquency'. | 因此，丛林和热带草原上不存在所谓的“青少年犯罪”。
[03:39.36]No necessity of making a living away from home results in neglect of children, and no father is confronted with his inability to 'buy' an education for his child. | 没有必须离家谋生的压力，因此孩子不会受到忽视；也没有父亲会因为无力为孩子“购买”教育而陷入困境。